#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180406} :activity/id #uuid "fa4e78d6-f3b0-503b-87cd-d288efaece3d" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050639 :topic/id #uuid "5b3a4c91-51d4-5634-a8c3-82457409b255" :topic/math-academy-id 3741} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180406 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180685 :tutorial/content "The range of a radical function $f(x)=\\sqrt[n]{x}$ depends on whether the index $n$ of the radical is even or odd. \n\nLet's start with the odd case first. What is the range of \n\n$$\nf(x) = -2\\sqrt[3]{3x-2}+2?\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the range of $y = \\sqrt[3] x$ is\n$y \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nTransformations do not change this interval. Therefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $y \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$" :tutorial/id #uuid "6b9dccc8-5bda-5458-a62d-5d74d82eb634" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4863 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "70a49b8b-925c-5999-90d0-2b2d817e962c" :step/math-academy-id 30458 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180410}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180407 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179684 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179543 :question/id #uuid "7096f867-7d37-5630-a885-d0a4f4a6acb7" :question/math-academy-id "e-8142"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e02202-ebdf-5987-bbaf-b5eb204c3892" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049986} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050642}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180300} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180303} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567026} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567080} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573914} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573921}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Radical Function With an Even Index"} :step/id #uuid "d6b1dfbb-7d27-561e-82ff-dafcb19e06f5" :step/math-academy-id 30459} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180410 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179687 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179546 :question/id #uuid "9af3bd0c-c209-508f-b806-bb9426f2c0da" :question/math-academy-id "e-8719"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abc2f98-9bbd-5a33-87fc-f9459fb18c60" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049528}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180301} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180302} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567030} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567090}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Radical Function With an Odd Index"} :step/id #uuid "f116d4fa-4115-5e01-a07f-ef9053e45179" :step/math-academy-id 32415 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180413}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180413 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180686 :tutorial/content "Let's now focus on the even case. What is the range of \n\n$$\ng(x) = -3\\sqrt[4]{2x-1}-2?\n$$\n\nThe range of $\\sqrt[4] x$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4] x \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply transformations to the inequality above to turn the left-hand side into $g(x).$\n\nFirst, remember that horizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{2x-1} \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-3$ and then subtracting $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{2x-1} & \\ge 0 \\\\ -3\\sqrt[4]{2x-1} & \\le 0 \\\\ -3\\sqrt[4]{2x-1}-2 & \\le -2 \\\\ g(x) & \\le -2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $g(x) \\in (-\\infty,-2].$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=g(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b7f3dc07cb72ea087d7cc4ec01379efa212b89fb8ab397b6df5bccfe75e66f5.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "a811e71d-0dee-5896-8be1-74b83f779ac4" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5199 :tutorial/title "The Range of a Transformed Radical Function With an Even Index"} :step/id #uuid "224fb34f-79c0-5dc1-b4cd-378542ebe04b" :step/math-academy-id 32637 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180407}}] :activity/title "The Range of a Transformed Radical Function" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179888}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573956} :activity/id #uuid "e5da4070-5ab5-5869-a280-ada7a6a61d1e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050639 :topic/id #uuid "5b3a4c91-51d4-5634-a8c3-82457409b255" :topic/math-academy-id 3741} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573956 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf0dcf63-fd14-596f-aeb9-5072df3edc97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y ∈ (- ∞, 4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179357} {:answer/id #uuid "c4c7e9be-9576-51d8-8cd3-3af543db209e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179358} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c9f8d0-5249-5c6c-bf41-d28b8afbc9d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y ∈ (- ∞, \\frac{3}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179359} {:answer/id #uuid "40b030d2-3ffb-53e5-8174-aea3a8f8a7fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y ∈ [- 4, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179360} {:answer/id #uuid "702005c5-a1fb-52ac-93d2-10c2c52e7aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y ∈ [- \\frac{3}{2}, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179361}] :answer-field/id #uuid "10ffbdef-349c-534b-bb9c-48e43d2f42d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e99ba81b-c0a5-5e2e-9652-4de0066a5c24" :question/math-academy-id "q-93038" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x) = 4\\sqrt[7]{3 - 2x}$?"} :step/id #uuid "28d87b32-1474-57af-8837-d988acdf430b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573971}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573967 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00256057-5438-57cd-9ec8-32eb432d8411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{7}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573421} {:answer/id #uuid "1e47d1d4-3d4b-5990-8852-84da67ed1aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573457} {:answer/id #uuid "4b15ece3-d0d6-5f29-9033-ac893c7f0278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in [\\frac{7}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573513} {:answer/id #uuid "f31cfaef-c698-5520-9e5a-a8bad3c27c9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573751} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2925b7-899a-5f43-86d7-9ca7119df9a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in [2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573768}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573751} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f4590d7-63a8-5906-9db9-e3c79e28fd23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c0ea79a6-c67e-5025-8851-d3340ce04b62" :question/math-academy-id "q-115847" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x)=-3\\sqrt[4]{2x-7}+2?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\sqrt[4]{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{2x-7}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-3$ and then adding $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{2x-7} & \\ge 0 \\\\ -3\\sqrt[4]{2x-7} & \\le 0 \\\\ -3\\sqrt[4]{2x-7}+2 & \\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,2].$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/e3/e39c45712a29b46df780efe37214aaafb3cb7ab1fa25072c4d9ca21a8bf6c731.png)"} :step/id #uuid "896ef864-228b-5e21-b144-577a92b10f1f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573971 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "060a50f3-17f0-5576-adec-3ba09c09188f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{4}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573430} {:answer/id #uuid "07381586-b8a1-5af8-95ad-a157695e9d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573431} {:answer/id #uuid "1c435279-0dd3-5a3c-a368-afe7f21e6ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573453} {:answer/id #uuid "3cdda6e7-9244-54c5-ab6a-91402d74d45e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in [2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573498} {:answer/id #uuid "4eed7b94-a229-54b1-857e-d360605e3623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\in [\\frac{4}{3},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573431} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e2bdc9-652d-56aa-ac6f-890e907f7f7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b3dce8b7-4368-5263-9706-4359213faf4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-98659" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x)=-4\\sqrt[6]{4-3x}+2?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\sqrt[6]{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[6]{x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[6]{4-3x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-4$ and then adding $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{4-3x} & \\ge 0 \\\\ -4\\sqrt[6]{4-3x} & \\le 0 \\\\ -4\\sqrt[6]{4-3x}+2 & \\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,2].$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/03/03804e230140549dd67834281d98130a0113122ded9d491b331d7ae76c621e93.png)"} :step/id #uuid "b1e386f4-59ca-5d77-b97f-dc5470bf3762" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573967}}] :activity/title "The Range of a Transformed Radical Function" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573418}]}
